From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pci: keep the certified ANS kexec handoff

Resetting the ANS host or its translations destroys the state required
by the next kernel. Describe the board-selected retained handoff.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
index f6497a4e1..f9b72ce26 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/apple,t8010-pcie.yaml
@@ -140,6 +140,10 @@ allOf:
         - apple,nvme-hmb
 
 properties:
+  apple,ans-kexec-handoff:
+    type: boolean
+    description: Retain storage port power across a certified stopped-DMA kexec handoff.
+
   compatible:
     oneOf:
       - enum:
